{"title":"2002 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2002 AMC 12B Problems\">2002 AMC 12B #4</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2002 AMC 10B Problems\">2002 AMC 10B #7</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(no_limits)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (no limits)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2.1_(faster_ending_to_solution_2)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2.1 (faster ending to solution 2)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3(similiar_to_solution2)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3(similiar to solution2)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> be a positive <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Integer\" title=\"Integer\">integer</a> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/7/1273d191f19d0ab5c49c782514ca380fd0c955b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac 12 + \\frac 13 + \\frac 17 + \\frac 1n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"119\" height=\"37\" /> is an integer. Which of the following statements is <b>not </b> true:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/8/4f874054cf8a01e4190218f922e9d6f8ad0d91e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A)}\\ 2\\ \\text{divides\\ }n \\qquad\\mathrm{(B)}\\ 3\\ \\text{divides\\ }n \\qquad\\mathrm{(C)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"320\" height=\"18\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/f/8af072b14326a50b63d6df1fe9f7b1584a7b71f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ 6\\ \\text{divides\\ }n  \\qquad\\mathrm{(D)}\\ 7\\ \\text{divides\\ }n \\qquad\\mathrm{(E)}\\ n &gt; 84$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"353\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/7/e77c293a88e8d47d1961dd65677b11b0d937d321.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac 12 + \\frac 13 + \\frac 17  = \\frac {41}{42}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"128\" height=\"37\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee13d3960646e8fe1105ba55176b7d41e6907a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 &lt; \\lim_{n \\rightarrow \\infty} \\left(\\frac{41}{42} + \\frac{1}{n}\\right) &lt; \\frac {41}{42} + \\frac 1n &lt; \\frac{41}{42} + \\frac 11 &lt; 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"354\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>From which it follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/f/4ff39a30da2a7dc4bec5b18746caba6d750d0346.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{41}{42} + \\frac 1n = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"91\" height=\"37\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/3/7d393526f55bac114397f85ee8e894d980bf9a87.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 42$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"12\" />. The only answer choice that is not true is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/7/8872b8480694c73aad321296b440a9d397127c88.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\mathrm{(E)}\\ n&gt;84}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"97\" height=\"29\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28no_limits.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(no_limits)\">Solution 2 (no limits)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (no limits)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/7/e77c293a88e8d47d1961dd65677b11b0d937d321.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac 12 + \\frac 13 + \\frac 17  = \\frac {41}{42}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"128\" height=\"37\" />, it is very clear that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/2/652902d9eae43fbacd2679da70d5ffb779a3776d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=42$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"12\" /> makes the expression an integer*. Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is a positive integer, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/d/83dacecc3f852b6d1fc31accf43e249930c0b27f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"13\" height=\"37\" /> must be less than or equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Thus, the only integer the expression can take is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, which means the only value for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/0/ed0d6c36fdad9c2874053be46c7e4120f2edcf47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$42$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />. Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/7/8872b8480694c73aad321296b440a9d397127c88.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\mathrm{(E)}\\ n&gt;84}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"97\" height=\"29\" />\n</p><p>~superagh\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2.1_.28faster_ending_to_solution_2.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2.1_(faster_ending_to_solution_2)\">Solution 2.1 (faster ending to solution 2)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2.1 (faster ending to solution 2)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Once you find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/2/652902d9eae43fbacd2679da70d5ffb779a3776d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=42$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"12\" />, you can skip the rest of Solution 2 by noting that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/e/60e75e11c152c3fcdba9c75edae83da375e8b058.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=42=2\\times3\\times7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"151\" height=\"15\" />, which satisfies A, B, C, D, but not E. Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/7/8872b8480694c73aad321296b440a9d397127c88.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\mathrm{(E)}\\ n&gt;84}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"97\" height=\"29\" /> must be the answer by PoE (Process of Elimination).\n</p><p><br />\n~speed tip by rawr3507\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3.28similiar_to_solution2.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3(similiar_to_solution2)\">Solution 3(similiar to solution2)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3(similiar to solution2)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Cross multiplying and adding the fraction we get the fraction to be equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/d/01dc973de93dc228c3671decae9afcbeb59c099b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac {41n + 42}{42n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"71\" height=\"37\" />, This value has to be an integer. This implies,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/0/470154aede13ecdb0e144bc6543784d36b29fa4d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$42n|(41n+42)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"116\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>=&gt; <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/1/bf1a59d4138d2efae59362ccaa6fb85174dbe168.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$42|(41n + 42)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"105\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<pre>  but <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/5/035a80dbb0cb36b5bb4218cb342458206aa98f0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$42|42$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"40\" height=\"18\" />, hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/7/4b70fcb878bb796f4cea1b89e89ab40818da662b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$42|41n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"18\" />\n  but <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/0/ed0d6c36fdad9c2874053be46c7e4120f2edcf47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$42$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> does not divides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/a/3ba6cdde56f366d628a7a35826f98523dbe58bd3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$41$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />,\n  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/a/11a466e02d0f5982114283cb2d3ece14a6473468.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$42|n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" />                                                                                                    -(1)\n</pre>\n<p>=&gt; <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/6/466821482f781db53e5c5460206cdfa6ee9fd3c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n|(41n+42)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"98\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<pre>  but <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/2/412653aad4dc64a33512038628f30acabfb012cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n|41n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"18\" />,\n  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/2/da2ca3d2da378cca3dd51fbfe3c55611511263e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n|42$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" />                                                                                                    -(2)\n</pre>\n<p>from (1) and (2) we get that n=42.\nComparing this with the options, we see that option E is the incorrect statement and hence E is the answer.\n</p><p>~rudolf1279\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10B\" title=\"2002 AMC 10B\">2002 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2002 AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2002 AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2002 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_8\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2002 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2002 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2002 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2002 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_4\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2002 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2002 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2002 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_7\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2002 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_8\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2002 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2002 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_10\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2002 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_11\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2002 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2002 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2002 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2002 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_15\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2002 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2002 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2002 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_18\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2002 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a h